 Track the phase in `manifest.json` `status` (`schemas/experiment-manifest.schema.json`). A skipped phase is marked `N/A` with the reason, never silently dropped.
 
+## Two tracks: pick one at intake
+
+| | **Track N — new idea, no tool yet** | **Track E — the tool already exists** |
+|---|---|---|
+| Steps | 0 → 1 → Gate A → 2 → 3 → 4 → 5 → 6 → 7 → 7b → 8 → Gate B | 0 → 4 → 5 (quick) → 6 → 7 → 7b → 8 → Gate B; steps 1-3 are `N/A (existing tool)` |
+| Planning (1-2: brief, design) | **Opus**, default effort | no new plan; a short `idea-brief.md` that names the question this run answers and links the previous run (baseline) |
+| Implement, tests, measurement (3, 4, 6, 7) | **Haiku 5.5, effort xhigh**, run as subagents with the haiku-subagent settings | same |
+| Review (5) | one read-only agent, Haiku 5.5 xhigh (Sonnet if the diff is large), given the brief, design, diff and test output | quick: same agent, given the current code and its tests only |
+| Improvement (7b) | **Opus**, default effort, one call per round | same |
+| Next round | an approved improvement starts a new experiment id in Track E | same |
+
+Track E never re-plans from scratch: it reads the last `improvements.md`, applies what the user approved, measures, and goes back to Opus only when the result is still bad (7b).
+
+## Token budget (applies to both tracks)
+
+Measured on the 2026-10-18 rounds: the orchestrating sessions and open-ended Opus agents cost about as much as all the Haiku case agents together. So:
+- **Opus is called with a closed input pack**: paste the numbers of `summary.json`, the last `improvements.md`, the diff or design change and the new results table into its prompt; tell it not to open files or explore the repo, and to answer in under 600 words. One call for planning (Track N), one call per improvement round (7b). No other Opus calls.
+- **Case agents**: Haiku 5.5, effort xhigh, at most 4 in flight per session, at most 2 measuring sessions on the machine at once (more made helpers time out and the numbers noisy). 4 cases × 2 repetitions unless the brief says otherwise.
+- **Keep every subagent under ~100k tokens of context**: small self-contained briefs, one fresh work folder, answers handed back short. The haiku-subagent skill's PreToolUse hook (`.claude/skills/haiku-subagent/tools/prompt-budget/subagent-hook.js`) trims a subagent's *starting prompt* to under 90k tokens; it does not compact a running subagent, and it only works when it is registered in `.claude/settings.json` (matcher `Agent|Task`). Check that before a run.
+- **Cheap checks before agent spend**: an offline gate (recall on gold tasks, a replay of recorded transcripts, a content run with `count_tokens.mjs`) runs first; the agent run starts only if the gate passes. Write the gate into `design.md` before running it.
+- **Few wake-ups for the orchestrator**: launch a batch of case agents, then end the turn or do other work; never poll, sleep or check status in a loop; collect a whole batch in one turn. Write outputs to files, keep chat short, and let the user `/compact` between phases of a long session.
+
